---
/*
 * DRAFT: to be reviewed by our lawyer before launch. Retention period (24 months) and response time (30 days)
 * to be confirmed.
 *
 * Written in plain English with India's Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 in mind.
 * This note is a code comment only and does not appear on the live page.
 * When you change the policy, update LAST_UPDATED below.
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHead from '../components/PageHead.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site.config.mjs';

const LAST_UPDATED = '20 November 2026';
const email = SITE.privacyEmail;
---

<Base
  title="Privacy policy | Salgotra Capital"
  description="How Salgotra Capital handles the details you share through this website, in plain English."
>
  <PageHead eyebrow="Privacy" title="Privacy policy" intro={`Last updated ${LAST_UPDATED}.`} />

  <section class="section on-light">
    <div class="container">
      <article class="policy measure">
        <p>
          This policy explains, in plain English, how Salgotra Capital ("we", "us") handles personal data that you
          share through this website. We follow India's Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023. For that law, we
          are the "Data Fiduciary" for the details you send us.
        </p>

        <h2>What we collect</h2>
        <p>We only collect what you choose to give us through the contact form:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>your name (required);</li>
          <li>a phone number or an email address, at least one of which is required;</li>
          <li>your business name and city (optional);</li>
          <li>anything you write about your business (optional);</li>
          <li>your agreement that we may use these details to reply to you.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We do not use advertising or tracking cookies, and we do not build profiles of visitors. Like any website,
          our hosting provider keeps basic technical logs (such as IP address and browser type) for a short time to
          keep the site secure and working.
        </p>

        <h2>Why we collect it</h2>
        <p>
          We use your details only to respond to your enquiry and, if you wish, to continue the conversation you
          started. We do not use them for marketing, and we do not add you to a mailing list.
        </p>

        <h2>Your consent</h2>
        <p>
          We process your details because you agree to it when you tick the consent box on the form. You can withdraw
          your consent at any time by emailing <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>. Withdrawing consent does not
          affect anything we did lawfully before you withdrew it, but we will stop using your details and delete them,
          unless the law requires us to keep them.
        </p>

        <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
        <p>
          We do not sell your details, and we do not share them with anyone else, except the service providers that
          run this website and its contact form (our website host and form service). They act only on our
          instructions, may store data on servers outside India, and may not use your details for their own purposes.
          We may also disclose details if the law requires it.
        </p>
        <p>
          If our conversation develops and you want us to involve independent chartered accountants or lawyers, we will only
          do so with your knowledge and under a duty of confidentiality.
        </p>

        <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
        <p>
          We keep enquiry details for as long as we are in conversation with you, and for up to 24 months after our
          last contact, so that we have a record if you return to us. After that we delete them. If you ask us to
          delete your details sooner, we will, unless the law requires us to keep them.
        </p>

        <h2>How we protect it</h2>
        <p>
          The site is served over an encrypted connection (HTTPS). Access to enquiries is limited to our directors. We
          take reasonable care to prevent loss, misuse or unauthorised access, and if a personal data breach affects
          you, we will tell you and the Data Protection Board of India as the law requires.
        </p>

        <h2>Your rights</h2>
        <p>You may ask us at any time to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>tell you what personal data we hold about you and how we use it;</li>
          <li>correct, complete or update your details;</li>
          <li>delete your details;</li>
          <li>name another person to exercise these rights for you in the event of death or incapacity.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          To make any of these requests, or if you have a concern, email <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>. We
          will reply as soon as we can, and in any case within 30 days. If you are not satisfied with our response,
          you may complain to the Data Protection Board of India.
        </p>

        <h2>Children</h2>
        <p>This website is meant for business owners and their advisors. We do not knowingly collect data from children.</p>

        <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>If we change this policy, we will update it on this page and change the date at the top.</p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Salgotra Capital, {SITE.location}.<br />
          Email: <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .policy h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 1.4rem + 0.7vw, 2rem);
    color: var(--ink);
    margin: 2.75rem 0 0.9rem;
    padding-top: 2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--umber) 22%, transparent);
  }
  .policy p + p,
  .policy ul + p,
  .policy p + ul {
    margin-top: 1em;
  }
  .policy ul {
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
  }
  .policy li + li {
    margin-top: 0.4em;
  }
  .policy li::marker {
    color: var(--bronze);
  }
</style>
